        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "98b24e9d-d38d-5534-b2a9-060462b62f4f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: Second Battle of Guam, First Battle of Guam, Battle of Antietam, Maryland Campaign\n- Places: Guam, Mariana Islands, Agat, Sharpsburg, Maryland, Antietam Creek\n- Organizations: United States, Japan\n- Topics: Pacific campaign, World War II\n\nFacts:\n- In 1862, the Battle of Antietam, also called the Battle of Sharpsburg especially in the South, was fought on September 17 near Sharpsburg, Maryland, and Antietam Creek as part of the Maryland Campaign.\n- In 1941, Japan captured Guam, a United States territory in the Mariana Islands, from the United States during the First Battle of Guam in the Pacific campaign of World War II.\n- From July 21 to August 10, 1944, the Second Battle of Guam was the American recapture of Japanese-held Guam.\n- In 1944, the beaches of Agat were one of the American landing sites in the Battle of Guam, during which Guam was retaken from occupying Japanese forces.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
